  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Sulphonates and quaternary ammonium salt of long chain fatty acids are used as synthetic detergents.</p><p>option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>16</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>COO</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is just a hydrocarbon chain which is insoluble in water.Hence, it is not a synthetic detergent.</p>",
    "image": null
